{"vehicles": [{"active_trouble_code_count": 11, "active_trouble_codes": [{"code": "P0522", "description": "Engine Oil Pressure Sensor/Switch Low", "detailed_description": "The Engine Oil Pressure Sensor tells the engine control module (PCM) the engine oil pressure. When the PCM detects an incorrect signal from this sensor it will set code P0522.The low oil warning light on the instrument cluster may also illuminated.", "reported": "2025-07-28T14:22:05.001000+00:00", "severity": 2}, {"code": "P0520", "description": "Engine Oil Pressure Sensor/Switch Circuit", "detailed_description": "The Engine Oil Pressure Sensor tells the engine control module (PCM) the engine oil pressure. When the PCM detects an incorrect signal from this sensor it will set code P0520.The low oil warning light on the instrument cluster may also illuminated.", "reported": "2025-07-25T12:48:03.001000+00:00", "severity": 2}, {"code": "P0481", "description": "Fan 2 Control Circuit", "detailed_description": "The purpose of the electric cooling fan system is to provide extra cooling capacity to the conventional radiator cooling system on hot days, and/or when the A/C is on, an/or when the vehicle is being driven in stop and go traffic which causes insufficient Airflow over the radiator. When the engine control module (PCM) cannot control the cooling fan as desired, it will set code P0481.", "reported": "2024-12-20T15:11:34.001000+00:00", "severity": 2}, {"code": "P2172", "description": "Throttle Actuator Control System - Sudden High Air Flow Detected", "detailed_description": "The electronic throttle control system (ETCS) controls the throttle valve opening. When the driver presses the accelerator pedal, the Accelerator Pedal Position Sensor (APP) sends a signal to the engine's control module (PCM) telling the PCM how much power the driver is requesting from the engine. The PCM then commands the throttle plate to open accordingly. If the PCM detects the sudden and excessive airflow through the engine, 