6", "description": "Evaporative Emission System Leak Detected (very small leak)", "detailed_description": "The evaporative control (EVAP) system captures any fuel vapors from the fuel tank and sends them through the vehicle's intake to be burned in the normal combustion process. When the engine control module detects a leak in this system, it will set code P0456.", "reported": "2023-03-15T11:42:50+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P0113", "description": "Intake Air Temperature Sensor 1 Circuit High", "detailed_description": "The Intake Air Temperature Sensor measures the air temperature going into the engine. The engine control module (PCM) uses this information to determine how much fuel to use to keep the engine running properly. When the PCM detects a problem with this sensor or the circuit for the sensor, it will set code P0113.", "reported": "2023-01-04T14:43:18+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P0135", "description": "O2 Sensor Heater Circuit", "detailed_description": "The purpose of the oxygen sensor is to measure the oxygen content in the exhaust gases after they leave the combustion process of the engine. The oxygen sensor must be at a certain temperature in order for this information to be accurate. The oxygen sensor has a heater wire inside to help bring the sensor up to temperature quicker. When the PCM detects the heater wire is not operating, it will set code P0135.", "reported": "2023-01-04T14:43:18+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P1299", "description": "Cylinder Head Temperature Sensor Detected Engine Overheating Condition", "detailed_description": "Each cylinder head on affected engines has a temperature sensor. When the engine's computer reads that a cylinder head temparture sensor is too high, it sets this code.", "reported": "2023-01-04T14:43:18+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P26B7", "description": "No description available for this code.", "detailed_description": null, "reported": "2023-01-04T14:43:18+00:00", "severity": null}], "battery_ch