cription": "The purpose of the oxygen sensor is to measure the oxygen content in the exhaust gases after they leave the combustion process of the engine. This information is critical to the PCM's ability to maintain efficient fuel economy. When the PCM detects a failure of the sensor or the information received from the sensor, it will set code P0138.", "reported": "2025-10-16T19:32:38.001000+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P0141", "description": "O2 Sensor Heater Circuit", "detailed_description": "The purpose of the oxygen sensor is to measure the oxygen content in the exhaust gases after they leave the combustion process of the engine. The oxygen sensor must be at a certain temperature in order for this information to be accurate. The oxygen sensor has a heater wire inside to help bring the sensor up to temperature quicker. When the PCM detects the heater wire is not operating, it will set code P0141.", "reported": "2024-08-29T17:57:41+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P0054", "description": "HO2S Heater Resistance", "detailed_description": "The purpose of the oxygen sensor is to measure the oxygen content in the exhaust gases after they leave the combustion process of the engine. The oxygen sensor must be at a certain temperature in order for this information to be accurate. The oxygen sensor has a heater wire inside to help bring the sensor up to temperature quicker. When the PCM detects the heater wire is not operating, it will set P0054.", "reported": "2024-08-29T17:31:54+00:00", "severity": 1}], "battery_charge_level": null, "battery_low": false, "battery_volts": 11.905033203125, "created": "2022-03-11T20:17:26.194872+00:00", "device_keys": ["agpzfnp1YmllY2FyciILEgZEZXZpY2UiFkZRb1hoeUo2eUp4anc2M2h5QTdlNXkM"], "driver": null, "fuel_economy": null, "fuel_economy_um": "mpg", "fuel_level": 19, "fuel_level_timestamp": "2026-01-29T20:45:32+00:00", "fuel_type": null, "group_keys": [], "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/zubie/image/fetch/https://d1ypc8j62c29y8.cloudfront.net/fullsize/2/9/b/9373786501333fd307afa32fe12edf77c67a7b92.png", "key": "agpzfnp1YmllY2FycjcLEgdBY2NvdW50IhZoSzQ2NThYaDJ5aENoaW13bVlZQ0hXDAsSA0NhciILQ1I1bjY5TFJMVHUM", "last_trip_key": "agpzfnp1YmllY2FyckILEgZEZXZpY2UiFkZRb1hoeUo2eUp4anc2M2h5QTdlNXkMCxIEVHJpcCIWS05Nd2oyUXJLb3ltQTZMcndBRlRCWQw", "make_name": "Ford", "mil_status": null, "model_name": "Transit Connect Cargo", "model_year": 2015, "nickname": "Truck 1", "odometer": 47415, "odometer_is_actual": false, "odometer_timestamp": "2026-01-29T20:45:56.001000+00:00", "odometer_um": "mi", "plate_expiration": null, "plate_jurisdiction": null, "plate_number": null, "primary_driver_key": null, "reported_vin": "NM0LS7E7XF1184045", "schedule_key": null, "style_fuel_capacity_gal": 15.8, "style_fuel_economy": 25.0, "style_fuel_economy_um": "mpg", "style_fuel_type": "Gasoline", "style_id": "400887601", "style_provider": "dataone", "style_url": null, "tag_keys": ["agpzfnp1YmllY2FyckILEgdBY2NvdW50IhZoSzQ2NThYaDJ5aENoaW13bVlZQ0hXDAsSA1RhZyIWZ0F5bUdoMkQ3dzd3S0Z5YjRLS0Y3egw"], "trim_name": "XL", "updated": "2026-02-06T12:38:17.167530+00:00", "vehicle_location": {"heading": null, "key": "agpzfnp1YmllY2FycicLEgtDYXJMb2NhdGlvbiIWUkVoRW9jR3VMYkg4M1UyUVpicUQ5WAw", "motion_status": "stopped", "point": {"lat": 25.646301, "lon": -80.407608}, "speed_mph": null, "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:38:10-05:00"}, "vin": "NM0LS7E7XF1184045"}, {"active_trouble_code_count": 5, "active_trouble_codes": [{"code": "P0138", "description": "O2 Sensor Circuit High Voltage", "detailed_description": "The purpose of the oxygen sensor is to measure the oxygen content in the exhaust gases after they leave the combustion process of the engine. This information is critical to the PCM's ability to maintain efficient fuel economy. When the PCM detects a failure of the sensor or the information received from the sensor, it will set code P0138.", "reported": "2024-07-26T13:09:43+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P2196", "description": "O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich", "detailed_description": "The Oxygen Sensor (or Air/Fuel Ratio Sensor) tells the engine control module how much oxygen is in the exhaust stream between the engine and the Catalytic Converter. The Oxygen Sensor's signal is supposed to fluctuate a minimum of 10 times per second within a specified range. If the engine's control module (PCM) determines that the Oxygen Sensor is not fluctuating throughout the normal range, the PCM will set code P2196.", "reported": "2024-06-14T13:24:54+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P0446", "description": "Evaporative Emission System Vent Control Circuit", "detailed_description": "The evaporative control (EVAP) system captures any fuel vapors from the fuel tank and sends them through the vehicle's intake to be burned in the normal combustion process. The EVAP Vent Valve allows fresh air to enter the EVAP system so it is not under a constant vacuum. When the engine control module (PCM) detects the evap system is venting when it should not, it will set code P0446.", "reported": "2024-06-03T17:25:34+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P1450", "description": "Unable to Bleed Up Fuel Tank Vacuum", "detailed_description": "The evaporative emissions system, which traps and stores fuel vapors until they can be properly burned and disposed of, may not release vacuum due to a possible vent valve concern. This can be due to damage to the charcoal canister due to overfilling fuel, or a concern in the related circuit or vent valve.", "reported": "2024-05-30T09:47:40+00:00", "severity": 1}, {"code": "P144A", "description": "This is a manufacturer-specific code. Contact your car dealer for more information on this code.", "detailed_description": null, "reported": "2024-04-03T12:55:27+00:00", "severity": null}], "battery_charge_level": null, "battery_low": false, "battery_volts": 12.2270400390625, "created": "2022-03-23T13:00:26.655644+00:00", "device_keys": ["agpzfnp1YmllY2FyciILEgZEZXZpY2UiFlFlclFjM0VzaHNFWTNTemFwaEJhSkgM"], "drive